# and a constructor has none - the type argument would have to come from what is
# handed in. So `SharedMut(0)` is the compiler's to type, the way `T?`'s `Some(…)`
# is (ADR-281 D2).
# A copy of what this value holds.
#
# What comes back is **stamped**: it carries where it came from, so a `set`
# that means *only if nothing changed since* can say which reading it means.
[fn."SharedMut::get"]
